read_diagnostics — resource-read tool mirror (DECIDED, planned)
===============================================================

status: DECIDED 2026-07-15, planned (wave TBD).
spec: "resource-read tool mirrors" under "mcp resources".
umbrella: plans/resource_tool_mirrors.

what it is: a builtin tool alias for the
isabelle://theory/{name}/diagnostics resource — errors/warnings with
positions from the current PIDE snapshot.

genuinely distinct from load_theory/check_theory: those (re)load and
report; read_diagnostics reads the CURRENT diagnostics across tiers
WITHOUT re-loading. keep it — it is not redundant with the theory tools.

advertised metadata (sketch)
----------------------------

name          read_diagnostics
description   "Read a theory's current errors and warnings with
              positions, without re-loading. Loaded theories answer
              from the live snapshot; image theories report \"checked
              at build time\"; filesystem-tier theories report \"not
              checked — load_theory to check\". Same content as the
              isabelle://theory/{name}/diagnostics resource."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {"theory": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["theory"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}

backing: zero new mechanism — the same theory_diagnostics path
(mcp_session.scala) the resource uses: image_theory normalization, the
three-tier answer (image / loaded via live snapshot / filesystem). one
function, two surfaces.

tests (sketch): [scala unit] row + dispatch + parity with the resource
read; [e2e] diagnostics of a loaded theory by tool and by resource,
byte-identical payloads.
